sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Cyanobacteria mat Turing ocellus wavelength at 64.19 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Re-run of the same checkpoint after the four Pass-1 gaps were closed in the script: narrow-band sweep (r = 0.999475), equal-diffusion ablation (sigma_max = -0.0588, RMS ratio 0.047), plate segmentation (137 colonies versus 65 spots, KS = 0.453), and eigenvector dispersion fit (r = 0.999986, RMSE = 0.00558) with the rejected bin-mean control still reported (r = 0.5288). cv_sim_similarity remains 90.7 on a 12-frame 640x520 GIF. The size distributions still disagree; that is measured, not tuned away. No second 64 µm micrograph and no second assessor. Overall 87.1. Overall 87.1/100 (faithfulness 86.4, reproducibility 88.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8c1db788ac0382399c6119652ec88de045be6725; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 89, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 89. Output judged: docs/media/cyanobacteria_mat_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 8c1db788ac0382399c6119652ec88de045be6725, image/png, 619956 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 29d2a0dd6b33420d9440717158f41c52cdeec9d201133dce28106873830495dc (sha256 29d2a0dd6b33420d9440717158f41c52cdeec9d201133dce28106873830495dc), spec_fingerprint 17c14d868777fb5a50af2e088b23ad6bf8798c31500d2ec6dec6508dc89f427c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 17c14d868777fb5a50af2e088b23ad6bf8798c31500d2ec6dec6508dc89f427c; artifact_sha256: 29d2a0dd6b33420d9440717158f41c52cdeec9d201133dce28106873830495dc; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/cyanobacteria_mat_turing_wavelength_s0/cyanobacteria_mat_holocene_culture_plate.jpg=858930a5ad520ee4..., datasets/cyanobacteria_mat_turing_wavelength_s0/cyanobacteria_mat_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=d166e23ba481aac8...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the existence of a selected finite wavenumber | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics | Petroff et al. 2010 centimetre-scale conical stromatolite spacing | Shepard and Sumner 2010 reticulate mats from filament motility; reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivities, including the measured finite-amplitude factor 1.08, so the saturated Fourier mode is 64.19 µm | Eigenvector single-mode growth rates, equal-diffusion ablation, and the diffusivity sweep | A display transfer that paints activator peaks as beige colonies on illuminated agar for comparison with the culture plate; transfer_boundary: The culture plate is macroscopic. Morphometrics that compare it to the 513.5 µm domain are scale-free (CV spectra, median-normalised diameters).; does_not_claim: That a paper measured 64.19 µm as a pigment wavelength of this mat | That the plate photograph is a 64 µm micrograph | That colony-size distributions match the spots (KS = 0.453) | That Petroff's cone equation is being integrated." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Closed: narrow-band sweep Pearson r = 0.999475 against lambda * sqrt(gamma).'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Closed: equal-diffusion sigma_max = -0.0588 and RMS ratio 0.047, printed on the comparison figure.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Closed: plate versus spot KS = 0.453 on median-normalised diameters. The distributions differ; the statistic is not a self-copy.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Closed: eigenvector probe Pearson r = 0.999986, RMSE = 0.00558. Rejected bin-mean r = 0.5288 remains in the metrics.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.871"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder and assessor, single-agent round)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

